item 1 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/1/measure".

item 1 measure is an assessment statement.

item 1 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 1 measure has the judgement "This Regulation is in line with Regulation (EC) No 223/2009 of the European Parliament and of the Council on European statistics. It represents a sectoral legislation that applies to the domain of European non-financial commercial real estate statistics.
This Regulation follows the recommendations of the Commission Recommendation (EU) 2023/397 of 17 February 2023 on reference metadata and quality reports for the European Statistical System.
This Regulation establishes a common minimum framework for the development, production and dissemination of a database on indicators regarding the physical commercial real estate market
The NSIs shall have the right to access and use, promptly and free of charge, all national administrative records, and to integrate those administrative records with statistics, to the extent necessary for the development and production of non-financial commercial real estate statistics.".

item 1 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure".

item 1 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 1 measure has the description "Assess the alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".


item 2 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/2/measure".

item 2 measure is an assessment statement.

item 2 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 2 measure has the judgement "According to Art. 5(4), the Commission is empowered to adopt implementing acts to specify elements of the data to be transmitted, and their technical definitions and simplifications.
According to Art. 6(4), The Commission is also empowered to adopt implementing acts to specify the details of the variables as well as the format, security and confidentiality measures and the procedure for the exchange of confidential data, the practical arrangements for the transmission, content of and deadlines for transmission of quality and metadata reports, the standards for data and metadata transmission, and relative derogations from the requirements of this Regulation.".

item 2 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure".

item 2 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 2 measure has the description "Assess the organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen".


item 3 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/measure".

item 3 measure is an assessment statement.

item 3 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 3 measure has the judgement "In line with Art. 6 of the regulation, reference metadata and quality reports will be available to improve the understanding of the European non-financial commercial real estate statistics;
Promotes the use of the Single Integrated Metadata Structure (SIMS and of international standards, such as the Statistical Data and Metadata Exchange (SDMX).".

item 3 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeSharedMeasure".

item 3 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 3 measure has the description "Assess the measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures".


item 4 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/4/measure".

item 4 measure is an assessment statement.

item 4 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 4 measure has the judgement "Promotes the use of established statistical or technical standards and infrastructure elaborated within the European Statistical System to the extent relevant for non-financial commercial real estate statistics.".

item 4 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeStandardsMeasure".

item 4 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 4 measure has the description "Assess the use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standardsPlease list such measures".


